---
import HomeLayout from '../../layouts/HomeLayout.astro';
import { beanReviews } from '../../data/bean-reviews';
import '../../styles/review.css';
import '../../styles/beans.css';
import '../../styles/bean-guides.css';
const date = '2026-10-15';
const path = '/coffee-beans/best-decaf-coffee-beans-by-brew-method/';
const canonical = 'https://coffeedant.com' + path;
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, '/');
const local = (path: string) => base + path.replace(/^\//, '');
const title = 'Best Decaf Coffee Beans by Brew Method';
const description = 'A research-led US guide to five exact decaf whole-bean coffees for espresso, drip, milk and mixed routines, with attributed notes, named processes and dated prices.';
const pickSpecs = [
  {slug:'/coffee-beans/intelligentsia-decaf-black-cat-espresso/',best:'Espresso-first',avoid:'You need a roaster drip recipe',method:'18 g in to 45 g finished espresso, per Intelligentsia',tradeoff:'The apple note may not suit a low-fruit espresso preference',process:'Water processed; provider not named'},
  {slug:'/coffee-beans/intelligentsia-organic-decaf-house-blend/',best:'Bright filter coffee',avoid:'You need a darker, low-citrus decaf',method:'1:18 coffee-to-water for pour-over or automatic drip',tradeoff:'Current washed Honduras record may change with future bags',process:'Water processed'},
  {slug:'/coffee-beans/stumptown-trapper-creek-decaf/',best:'One bag for drip and espresso',avoid:'You require published component origins',method:'Stumptown provides separate drip and espresso starts',tradeoff:'A switchable grinder and two saved settings are needed',process:'Swiss Water Process'},
  {slug:'/coffee-beans/counter-culture-slow-motion-decaf/',best:'Medium, cocoa-led multi-method use',avoid:'You demand a fixed lot or guaranteed low acidity',method:'Counter Culture lists an 18 g, roughly 1:2 espresso start',tradeoff:'Blend components and independent sample impressions vary',process:'Swiss Water unless lot states otherwise'},
  {slug:'/coffee-beans/equator-decaf-equator-blend/',best:'Current origin and process detail',avoid:'You chiefly want an exact espresso recipe',method:'Separate Equator drip, Chemex and French press starts',tradeoff:'No comparably specific espresso target on checked page',process:'Mountain Water Process'}
];
const picks = pickSpecs.map((spec) => ({...spec, review: beanReviews.find((review) => review.slug === spec.slug)!}));
const sections = [
  {id:'framework',title:'Choose by the drink, then the decaf method',paragraphs:[
    'We included current US whole-bean products with an exact roaster listing, a named or at least described decaffeination route, a useful brew role, a verified 12 oz price and a full Coffeedant review. We excluded instant coffee, pods, half-caff blends, sold-out lots and products whose exact identity could not be checked. These five are not a blind sensory ranking: each solves a different purchase decision. [1] [2] [3] [4] [5]',
    'Start with the brewer you use most. Intelligentsia Decaf Black Cat gives a specific espresso dose and output. Organic Decaf House gives a filter ratio. Stumptown explicitly discusses both espresso and drip. Counter Culture publishes several brew methods and its changing blend history. Equator gives unusually detailed current component origins and several filter recipes. A nominally versatile bag cannot make one grind setting work for espresso and drip.',
    'We did not reward the most vivid flavor copy. Cocoa, apple, lime, citrus, graham, molasses and nutmeg are words from roasters, not Coffeedant tasting notes. Independent sample reviews and owner posts add bounded perspective where available, but their roast dates and recipes can differ from the bag delivered to you. Read the linked full reviews for each source and uncertainty.'
  ]},
  {id:'caffeine',title:'Water-process claims do not mean zero caffeine',paragraphs:[
    'Swiss Water is named on the Stumptown listing and on Counter Culture Slow Motion unless otherwise noted for the lot. Equator names Mountain Water. Intelligentsia says its two products are water processed, without naming a processing provider on the checked product pages. These are product and process disclosures, not proof that the five cups have equal residual caffeine or equal flavor. [1] [2] [3] [4] [5]',
    'The US FDA says an eight-fluid-ounce cup of brewed decaf typically contains 2–15 mg caffeine. That range is useful context, but cannot be applied as a measurement of a specific coffee, espresso shot or serving. Swiss Water itself says residual caffeine in a brewed cup varies with dose and method. Buyers who need exact exposure should seek product-specific information and professional advice for their own situation. [6] [7]',
    'A label calling water processing “chemical-free” describes the absence of added chemical solvents in that commercial process; water and the beans are still physical substances. We use the named method, not an implied health or sensory superiority. The best-for choices below follow documented brewing use and transparent buying facts.'
  ]},
  {id:'recipes',title:'Espresso and filter need separate evidence',paragraphs:[
    'Intelligentsia recommends 18 g coffee to 45 g finished espresso for Decaf Black Cat. That 1:2.5 ratio is a useful start if your basket can hold the dose. It is not a promise that a shot takes a particular number of seconds on your grinder. Its Organic Decaf House page instead recommends 1 g coffee to 18 g water for drip or pour-over. For a 20 g filter dose, that arithmetic gives 360 g water. Do not copy the filter ratio into a portafilter. [3] [4]',
    'Stumptown gives a separate 1:17 drip starting ratio and an espresso preparation near 19.5 g. Counter Culture gives an 18 g espresso start around 1:2. Equator gives drip near 1:15, Chemex 1:16 and French press near 1:15. These are roaster recipe starting points, not Coffeedant extractions. Use your actual basket, water and grinder; save dose, yield and setting so each later bag can be assessed. [1] [2] [5]',
    'If a household alternates regular and decaf, a hopper can retain beans and the grinding path can retain grounds. If it also alternates espresso and drip, you need repeatable adjustment. Those workflow costs may matter more than a small difference in 12 oz bag price. Our grinder reviews can help choose a setup, but no grinder automatically makes an unsuitable flavor direction fit.'
  ]},
  {id:'freshness',title:'Test 12 oz before committing to five pounds',paragraphs:[
    'All five had a 12 oz whole-bean option in the official product feeds on October 15, 2026. Counter Culture also listed 24 oz; Equator listed 2 lb; several listed 5 lb. A larger bag lowers the arithmetic price per gram in some feeds but adds a freshness obligation. A product photo and online stock flag do not tell you the roast date of the bag that arrives. Check the bag or ask the seller. [1] [2] [3] [4] [5]',
    'Store an opened working bag sealed in a cool, dry place, away from moisture and odors. Stumptown cautions against repeatedly moving opened beans into and out of the freezer. If you use only an evening decaf several times a week, calculate grams per week before choosing a bulk bag. The real value of a large pack falls quickly when half goes stale or the flavor brief proves wrong for your brewer. [8] [9]',
    'For a first trial, brew several cups with one 12 oz bag and a written recipe. Note the roast date, process disclosure, selected size, grinder setting and what you personally liked. This is a suggested reader exercise, not a claim that Coffeedant sampled the products.'
  ]},
  {id:'value',title:'Compare the same pack and currency',paragraphs:[
    'The verified US direct 12 oz base prices on October 15 were $18.50 for each Intelligentsia bag, $19.50 for Equator, and $20 for Counter Culture and Stumptown. Shipping, tax, subscriptions, promotions and checkout availability were not included. A 12 oz bag contains about 340 g; at an illustrative 18 g dose that is about nineteen theoretical doses before dial-in waste. Price differences of $1–$1.50 per bag are less useful than buying a flavor direction and brew role you will finish. [1] [2] [3] [4] [5]',
    'A 5 lb option can be rational for a café or a high-use household, but only after the 12 oz trial establishes the recipe and consumption rate. Do not compare one roaster’s 12 oz price to another’s 5 lb unit price without accounting for use, storage and shipping. Direct and grocery stock may have different dates; verify the seller and actual bag.',
    'The external DecafLife reviews cover older samples of Slow Motion and Decaf House. They inform expectations but do not justify moving a current product above another in a ranked tasting list. Equator’s external specification-led overview expressly did not taste that coffee. The ordering here is by use case, not a numeric sensory score. [10] [11] [12]'
  ]},
  {id:'alternatives',title:'When these five are the wrong shortlist',paragraphs:[
    'If your goal is a dark roast regardless of caffeine, the existing dark-roast guide addresses that separate choice. If you want a fixed origin and variety, a current single-origin decaf with a fully documented lot could be better than these recurring blends; verify current stock and process before buying. If you need a half-caff routine, none of these five is a half-caff product. [13]',
    'If a very low-citrus profile is essential, examine the roaster notes before choosing Trapper Creek, Organic Decaf House or Decaf Black Cat. Their citrus, lime or apple directions are not guarantees of acidity but are reasonable selection signals. For a bigger milk drink, Stumptown explicitly says Trapper Creek carries in milk; Equator says its blend is designed for black coffee or a splash of milk. Those claims do not prove how a particular latte will taste. [2] [3] [4] [5]',
    'Keep the first decision small. Buy the exact 12 oz product that has evidence for your main brew, record a recipe, then compare your own result against an alternative only after you know what you wanted to change.'
  ]}
];
const faqs = [
  {q:'Is decaf coffee completely caffeine-free?',a:'No. The FDA gives a typical 2–15 mg per eight-fluid-ounce brewed cup; this guide does not measure any specific product or serving.'},
  {q:'Which pick has the clearest espresso recipe?',a:'Intelligentsia Decaf Black Cat publishes an 18 g in to 45 g out starting point. Check your basket and dial in the actual bag.'},
  {q:'Which pick is most clearly aimed at filter?',a:'Intelligentsia Organic Decaf House names drip and pour-over and gives a 1:18 starting ratio.'},
  {q:'Can one decaf bag work for espresso and drip?',a:'Stumptown explicitly positions Trapper Creek for both, and Counter Culture offers method-specific guidance. Save two grind settings and recipes.'},
  {q:'Are these Coffeedant tasting winners?',a:'No. These are research-led best-for picks based on exact identity, roaster use, dated price and evidence limits. Coffeedant has not tasted them.'},
  {q:'Why start with 12 oz?',a:'A small bag tests freshness, flavor preference and grinder workflow before bulk size increases the risk of waste.'},
  {q:'Does the listed price include delivery?',a:'No. US direct base prices were checked October 15, 2026; shipping, tax, subscriptions and checkout stock can change.'}
];
const sources = [
  ['Counter Culture Slow Motion','https://counterculturecoffee.com/products/12-oz-slow-motion','Blend, process, method and official variant feed checked October 15.'],
  ['Stumptown Trapper Creek','https://www.stumptowncoffee.com/products/trapper-creek-decaf','Swiss Water, multi-method claims, recipes and official variant feed checked October 15.'],
  ['Intelligentsia Decaf Black Cat','https://www.intelligentsia.com/products/decaf-black-cat-espresso','Water process, roaster notes, espresso target and official variant feed checked October 15.'],
  ['Intelligentsia Organic Decaf House','https://www.intelligentsia.com/products/decaf-house-blend','Current washed Honduras panel, roaster notes, filter recipe and official variant feed checked October 15.'],
  ['Equator Decaf Equator Blend','https://www.equatorcoffees.com/collections/decaf/products/decaf-equator-blend','Current components, Mountain Water, brewing and official variant feed checked October 15.'],
  ['US FDA: caffeine in decaf','https://www.fda.gov/consumers/consumer-updates/spilling-beans-how-much-caffeine-too-much','Typical brewed-decaf range, not an assay of the five products.'],
  ['Swiss Water residual-caffeine context','https://www.swisswater.com/blogs/sw/how-much-caffeine-is-in-decaf','Process-provider context and variation by dose and brew.'],
  ['Stumptown freshness advice','https://support.stumptowncoffee.com/hc/en-us/articles/5550819144461-How-long-does-Stumptown-coffee-stay-fresh','Roaster freshness context.'],
  ['Stumptown storage advice','https://support.stumptowncoffee.com/hc/en-us/articles/5568076789901-Where-should-I-store-my-coffee-In-the-freezer-On-the-counter','General moisture and freezer cautions.'],
  ['DecafLife Slow Motion sample','https://decaflife.com/coffee-reviews/counter-culture-slow-motion-decaf/','Older independent sample, not a current-lot result.'],
  ['DecafLife Decaf House sample','https://decaflife.com/coffee-reviews/intellegentsias-decaf-house-roast-review/','Older independent sample, not a current-lot result.'],
  ['Coffee Guru Equator overview','https://thecoffeeguru.net/beans/equator-decaf-equator-blend','Specification-led external overview that discloses no hands-on test.'],
  ['Coffeedant dark-roast guide','https://coffeedant.com/coffee-beans/best-dark-roast-coffee-beans/','Separate caffeine-neutral dark-roast decision.']
];
const cite = (p: string) => p.replace(/\[(\d+)\]/g, (_m,n) => '<a class="bean-cite" href="#s' + n + '" aria-label="Source ' + n + '">[' + n + ']</a>');
const author = {'@type':'Person',name:'Aleksandar Spasevski',jobTitle:'Editor, Coffeedant',url:'https://coffeedant.com/about/',image:'https://coffeedant.com/images/author-aleksandar-spasevski.jpg'};
const schema = {'@context':'https://schema.org','@graph':[
  {'@type':'Article','@id':canonical+'#article',headline:title,description,genre:'Research-led coffee buying guide',inLanguage:'en-US',datePublished:date,dateModified:date,author,mainEntityOfPage:canonical,image:picks.map(p=>p.review.image),citation:sources.map(s=>s[1]),publisher:{'@type':'Organization',name:'Coffeedant',url:'https://coffeedant.com/'}},
  {'@type':'ItemList','@id':canonical+'#shortlist',name:'Decaf beans by brew method',itemListElement:picks.map((p,i)=>({'@type':'ListItem',position:i+1,name:p.review.roaster+' '+p.review.coffee,url:'https://coffeedant.com'+p.slug}))},
  {'@type':'BreadcrumbList',itemListElement:[{'@type':'ListItem',position:1,name:'Home',item:'https://coffeedant.com/'},{'@type':'ListItem',position:2,name:'Coffee beans',item:'https://coffeedant.com/coffee-beans/'},{'@type':'ListItem',position:3,name:title,item:canonical}]},
  {'@type':'FAQPage',mainEntity:faqs.map(f=>({'@type':'Question',name:f.q,acceptedAnswer:{'@type':'Answer',text:f.a}}))}
]};
---
<HomeLayout title={title + ' | Coffeedant'} description={description} canonicalPath={path} image={picks[0].review.image} imageAlt="Official Intelligentsia Decaf Black Cat coffee bag" ogType="article" published={date} updated={date}>
  <main id="main-content" class="review-page bean-buying-guide" data-guide-kind="coffee-beans">
    <div class="review-shell">
      <nav class="review-breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href={base}>Home</a><span>/</span><a href={local('/coffee-beans/')}>Coffee beans</a><span>/</span><span>Decaf by brew</span></nav>
      <header class="bean-guide-header">
        <p class="review-overline">Coffee buying guide · research-led · United States</p>
        <h1>{title}</h1>
        <p class="bean-lead">Choose the decaf that documents your main brewer. These five exact whole-bean products have different reasons to buy; none has a Coffeedant sensory score.</p>
        <aside class="review-author-card"><div class="review-author-head"><img src={local('/images/author-aleksandar-spasevski.jpg')} alt="Aleksandar Spasevski, editor at Coffeedant" width="46" height="46" /><div><strong>Aleksandar Spasevski</strong><small>Editor, Coffeedant</small></div></div><p>Published and checked <time datetime={date}>October 15, 2026</time> · US direct-purchase context</p><p>I checked current roaster listings, official product feeds, decaf processes, recipes, freshness advice and external reports. I have not bought, brewed or tasted these coffees. Best-for labels are editorial buying judgments.</p></aside>
      </header>
      <nav class="bean-jump" aria-label="Guide sections"><strong>Decide by your brew</strong>{sections.map(s=><a href={'#'+s.id}>{s.title}</a>)}<a href="#quick-compare">Quick comparison</a><a href="#picks">The picks</a><a href="#detailed-compare">Detailed comparison</a><a href="#faq">FAQ</a><a href="#sources">Sources</a></nav>
      <article class="bean-article">
        {sections.slice(0,2).map(s=><section class="review-section" id={s.id}><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">Selection method</p><h2>{s.title}</h2></header><div class="review-section-body">{s.paragraphs.map(p=><p set:html={cite(p)} />)}</div></section>)}
        <section class="review-section" id="quick-compare"><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">Five different buying reasons</p><h2>Quick comparison</h2></header><div class="bean-guide-table" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Scrollable decaf coffee comparison"><table><caption>Exact US 12 oz whole-bean products; base prices checked October 15, 2026</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Coffee</th><th scope="col">Best for</th><th scope="col">12 oz base price</th><th scope="col">Skip if</th></tr></thead><tbody>{picks.map(p=><tr><th scope="row"><a href={local(p.slug)}>{p.review.roaster} {p.review.coffee}</a></th><td>{p.best}</td><td>{p.review.price}</td><td>{p.avoid}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></section>
        <section class="review-section" id="picks"><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">Read the exact full review</p><h2>Match the decaf to the main drink</h2></header><div class="bean-index-grid">{picks.map(p=><article class="bean-guide-pick"><img src={p.review.image} alt={p.review.imageAlt} width="360" height="360" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><div><p class="review-overline">{p.best}</p><h3><a href={local(p.slug)}>{p.review.roaster} {p.review.coffee}</a></h3><p><strong>Roaster notes:</strong> {p.review.facts.find(f=>f.label==='Roaster flavor notes')?.value}.</p><p><strong>Method evidence:</strong> {p.method}.</p><p><strong>Tradeoff:</strong> {p.tradeoff}.</p><p><strong>Think twice:</strong> {p.avoid}.</p><p class="bean-credit"><a href={p.review.officialUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Image: {p.review.roaster}</a>. Official bag-identification photograph.</p><a class="bean-guide-review-link" href={local(p.slug)}>Read the full review →</a></div></article>)}</div></section>
        <section class="review-section" id="detailed-compare"><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">Process and workflow</p><h2>Detailed buying comparison</h2></header><div class="bean-guide-table" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Scrollable detailed decaf comparison"><table><caption>Roaster claims and dated base prices; no measured caffeine or sensory ranking</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Factor</th>{picks.map(p=><th scope="col"><a href={local(p.slug)}>{p.review.coffee}</a></th>)}</tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Decaf process</th>{picks.map(p=><td>{p.process}</td>)}</tr><tr><th scope="row">Brew evidence</th>{picks.map(p=><td>{p.method}</td>)}</tr><tr><th scope="row">Current origin</th>{picks.map(p=><td>{p.review.facts.find(f=>f.label==='Current origin')?.value}</td>)}</tr><tr><th scope="row">12 oz price</th>{picks.map(p=><td>{p.review.price}; US direct, Oct 15</td>)}</tr><tr><th scope="row">Main limit</th>{picks.map(p=><td>{p.tradeoff}</td>)}</tr></tbody></table></div></section>
        {sections.slice(2).map(s=><section class="review-section" id={s.id}><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">Make a repeatable choice</p><h2>{s.title}</h2></header><div class="review-section-body">{s.paragraphs.map(p=><p set:html={cite(p)} />)}</div></section>)}
        <section class="review-section" id="related"><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">Related buying decisions</p><h2>Explore the adjacent choices</h2></header><div class="bean-alternatives"><a href={local('/coffee-beans/best-dark-roast-coffee-beans/')}><strong>Dark-roast coffee guide</strong><span>Choose a developed roast regardless of caffeine.</span></a><a href={local('/coffee-beans/best-coffee-beans-for-espresso-and-drip/')}><strong>Espresso and drip guide</strong><span>Compare regular-caffeine dual-method coffees.</span></a><a href={local('/grinder/')}><strong>Grinder reviews</strong><span>Evaluate grind switching and regular-to-decaf workflow.</span></a></div></section>
        <section class="review-section" id="methodology"><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">Evidence and limits</p><h2>How this shortlist was built</h2></header><div class="review-section-body"><p>This is a research-led US selection based on current official product identity, brew role, process disclosure, 12 oz availability and dated base price. Independent sample reports and owner accounts are attributed and treated as limited to those bags and brewers. Coffeedant did not taste, brew, measure caffeine, or rank these products by sensory quality. No affiliate link is required to read the full reviews.</p><p>Prices were checked October 15, 2026 in official roaster product feeds. Tax, shipping, subscriptions, discounts, future lots and checkout stock are outside this comparison. Check the current bag and seller before purchase.</p></div></section>
        <section class="review-section" id="faq"><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">Quick answers</p><h2>Decaf coffee FAQ</h2></header><div class="bean-faq">{faqs.map(f=><article><h3>{f.q}</h3><p>{f.a}</p></article>)}</div></section>
        <section class="review-section" id="sources"><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">Trace the claims</p><h2>Sources</h2></header><ol class="review-source-list">{sources.map((s,i)=><li id={'s'+(i+1)}><a href={s[1]} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{s[0]} ↗</a><p>{s[2]} Checked October 15, 2026.</p></li>)}</ol></section>
        <section class="final-verdict"><p class="review-overline">The first useful bag</p><h2>Pick for the brew you make most</h2><p>Buy one 12 oz whole-bean bag whose roaster documentation matches your main method. Save a recipe and check the delivered roast date. Only then decide whether another decaf, a different grinder routine or a larger pack would improve the next purchase.</p><a class="review-buy-button review-buy-button-dark" href={local('/coffee-beans/')}>Explore all bean reviews →</a></section>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
  <script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema).replace(/</g, '\\u003c')} />
</HomeLayout>
